 "notes": "Rows for Kyaukpyu, Sandoway and Rangoon (first row) print the mother tongue as 'Do.' (= Other Tibeto-Burmese languages); expanded, with the printed form noted in mother_tongue. Hanthawaddy prints 'Languages of the Tai Group' (without '(Shan)'). Table continues on leaf 241. Part II Bilingualism (printed pages 234-235): rows = district x mother-tongue group; cols 3-4 total number of speakers of that mother tongue (M/F); cols 5-14 number speaking a subsidiary language in each group (M/F). No Persons column. Each row is emitted as one record per subsidiary group with non-nil figures (total_males/total_females repeat the col 3-4 totals); a row with no subsidiary figures at all is emitted once with subsidiary=null so the total is kept. Self-checks: subsidiary sums never exceed totals; totals for Burma, Karen and Tai mother tongues equal the I-D group figures for that district, and Mon-Khmer totals equal I-D Mon (K) + Palaung-Wa (L) (all pass)."
